00:08:48,440 --> 00:08:50,160
That post is titled Why Scouting.

130
00:08:50,160 --> 00:08:56,840
It's still up. it's still there on the blog and I'll link to it in the podcast notes.

131
00:08:56,840 --> 00:09:03,960
The first podcast, the first scoutmaster podcast, was published on January 25th 2010, which happens

132
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:06,680
to be exactly five years ago today.

133
00:09:06,680 --> 00:09:10,920
When I started the blog, I'd been a scoutmaster for just over 25 years.

134
00:09:10,920 --> 00:09:17,000
I started at the very young age of 24. in 1984, believe it or not,

135
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:22,160
10 years ago- I decided I wanted to start writing about what I had learned about scouting.

136
00:09:22,160 --> 00:09:28,560
I wanted to encourage the BSA to make some changes and I wanted to write about those.

137
00:09:28,560 --> 00:09:32,040
And some of those changes have come to pass. others still are waiting.

138
00:09:32,040 --> 00:09:36,760
But right now, all told, I've been volunteering for the BSA- for I haven't really stopped

139
00:09:36,760 --> 00:09:41,680
to count, but it's probably close on maybe 37,, 38 years.

140
00:09:41,680 --> 00:09:46,000
I've worked at the unit level with Cub Scouts. I've been a Weeblos Den Leader. I've

141
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:48,840
been a Cub Master, an Assistant Cub Master.

142
00:09:48,840 --> 00:09:51,480
Like I said, I've been a scoutmaster.

143
00:09:51,480 --> 00:09:54,560
Right now I am a Venture Crew Advisor.

144
00:09:54,560 --> 00:09:58,400
I've worked at the district and the council level and I have a fairly wide experience

145
00:09:58,400 --> 00:10:01,880
of the Boy Scouts of America as an organization.

146
00:10:01,880 --> 00:10:05,040
But, as I've said in the past, you know that's what we are right,

147
00:10:05,040 --> 00:10:08,320
That's what the BSA is. it's an organization.

148
00:10:08,320 --> 00:10:15,000
The BSA is not- quote- scouting unquote- it's an organization that contains scouting.

149
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:22,320
My subject and what I want to promote and grow is scouting rather than just an organization.

150
00:10:22,320 --> 00:10:27,000
Baden Powell pointed out: we are a movement rather than an organization,

151
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:29,920
And there's a lot of differences between those two things.

152
00:10:29,920 --> 00:10:33,120
For the past 10 years, I've been privileged to connect with

153
00:10:33,120 --> 00:10:34,520
scouts all over the world

154
00:10:34,520 --> 00:10:38,920
And one thing I know for certain is: regardless of what organization

155
00:10:38,920 --> 00:10:43,840
we're serving in, we all experience the same challenges and we all achieve the

156
00:10:43,840 --> 00:10:48,640
same victories and we share the same aim, and that very simple aim is to help young

157
00:10:48,640 --> 00:10:53,240
people, and the principles of scouting apply no matter where you are.

158
00:10:53,240 --> 00:10:57,200
As everybody grew more familiar with the internet in the past couple of decades,

159
00:10:57,200 --> 00:10:59,480
scouters were very early adopters.

160
00:10:59,480 --> 00:11:05,040
There were web pages and listserv started and later on, blogs and then podcasts,

161
00:11:05,040 --> 00:11:07,800
and a lot of those things have come and gone.

162
00:11:07,800 --> 00:11:12,880
I'm kind of amazed that 10 years later, this has been so compelling and so

163
00:11:12,920 --> 00:11:16,360
interesting and useful for me that I'm still here talking to you.

164
00:11:16,360 --> 00:11:17,480
How about that?

165
00:11:17,480 --> 00:11:21,040
I mean, I am constantly amazed by the potential of tools that we have in our

166
00:11:21,040 --> 00:11:25,920
hands now to allow us to share and inform and to work together.

167
00:11:25,920 --> 00:11:30,640
It's been challenging and it's been very exhilarating trying to sort all of

168
00:11:30,640 --> 00:11:33,400
these things out, all of this technology.

169
00:11:33,400 --> 00:11:37,040
Some things have tried to work pretty well, some things didn't,

170
00:11:37,040 --> 00:11:40,320
And that brings me around to what I wanted to talk about

171
00:11:40,320 --> 00:11:43,640
And that's what I ought to stop doing and what I ought to continue doing

172
00:11:43,640 --> 00:11:46,120
And some things that I need to start doing

173
00:11:47,240 --> 00:11:51,160
Now. stop doing thing is a fairly short list, because I've tried and

174
00:11:51,160 --> 00:11:54,040
abandoned a few things over the past already.

175
00:11:54,040 --> 00:11:57,520
I'll say the single test I used to evaluate what to stop doing is whether

176
00:11:57,520 --> 00:12:00,480
it seems to be helping folks to be better scouters.

177
00:12:00,480 --> 00:12:03,000
If it works, I want to keep doing it.

178
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:07,400
And there's also like the question of is it working for enough people?

179
00:12:07,400 --> 00:12:10,800
Because there's a significant amount of time and resources that you put into this.

180
00:12:10,800 --> 00:12:15,720
So I'm not necessarily concerned about having the biggest audience in the world,

181
00:12:15,720 --> 00:12:17,760
But am I getting through?

182
00:12:17,760 --> 00:12:20,160
That's really kind of the test for a lot of this.

183
00:12:20,160 --> 00:12:24,520
The only really substantial thing I'm going to stop doing this coming year

184
00:12:24,520 --> 00:12:27,640
is supporting the Scoutmaster CG app.

185
00:12:27,640 --> 00:12:30,840
If you didn't know that, I had one so much. the better

186
00:12:30,840 --> 00:12:34,480
Apps turn out to be very costly and getting them right and

187
00:12:34,480 --> 00:12:37,000
maintaining them is very time consuming

188
00:12:37,040 --> 00:12:41,480
And I think there are really better things to devote the time and resources to.

189
00:12:41,480 --> 00:12:45,680
If you have the app uploaded on a mobile device and find it useful,

190
00:12:45,680 --> 00:12:49,120
it'll likely continue to work,

